meta {
  name: Presign Service Document (as CSR)
  type: http
  seq: 58
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carrier-reconciliation/assigned/{{reconRowId}}/documents/presign
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{reconSvcCsrToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "filename": "morgan-hale-application.pdf",
    "contentType": "application/pdf",
    "size": 2048
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setVar("reconSvcKey", res.getBody().key);
    bru.setVar("reconSvcUploadUrl", res.getBody().uploadUrl);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("a key under the row", function () {
    const key = res.getBody().key;
    expect(key).to.contain(`/reconciliation-rows/${bru.getVar("reconRowId")}/nba/`);
    expect(res.getBody().uploadUrl).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /carrier-reconciliation/assigned/:rowId/documents/presign — the 1-800 policy's application

  - **Module:** `carrier_reconciliation` (enabled for the agency)
  - **Permission:** `carrier_reconciliation:read` **or** `leads:read` — the
    assignee's class gate; no `:write` (the service clamps to the assignee)
  - **Data scope:** the row's assignee only

  PAC-173 PR 5. A presigned PUT for the signed **new business application** a
  service intake attaches — required, a PDF, as on every policy entered. Its
  own endpoint because the Sold form's (`POST /sold-deals/documents/presign`)
  is anchored on a lead and needs `deal_audits:write`, and a service intake
  makes no lead and is done by CSRs. The key is
  `agencies/<agencyId>/reconciliation-rows/<rowId>/nba/<year>/<uuid>-<file>`,
  so the prefix is the ownership check: `Service Intake` refuses a key for
  another row. Feeds `Upload Service Document`.

  ## Body
  - `filename` — 1–255 characters
  - `contentType` — `application/pdf` only
  - `size` — bytes, ≤ 10 MB

  ## Response `201`
  `{ key, uploadUrl, requiredHeaders, expiresIn }` — PUT the bytes to
  `uploadUrl` with `requiredHeaders` and no `Authorization`.

  ## Errors
  - `400` — validation (not a PDF, too large);
    `RECONCILIATION_OUTCOME_NOT_ALLOWED` — the row offers no service intake
  - `404` — no such row, or it is not assigned to the caller
}
